        ("scope", "CEDAR EQUIPMENT TRUST | CASH MEMORANDUM CE-9 | 2026-09-01\nThis is a fictional closed trust, not a public investment offer. Amounts in the exercise are thousands of CNY. Interest targets are accounting obligations for a period, not guaranteed returns. A trustee fee cap and the reserve target are separate limits."),
        ("pool", "DISTRIBUTABLE CASH\nBegin with period collections plus the opening unrestricted cash balance. Exclude money held in the tax escrow and exclude unreceived sale proceeds. A signed equipment sale contract is not collected cash. Restricted reserve cash is separate from the opening unrestricted balance and is not added a second time."),
        ("waterfall", "NORMAL WATERFALL\nApply distributable cash in this order: (1) trustee fee, capped at 5 each period; (2) senior current interest and senior interest arrears; (3) refill the liquidity reserve to its target; (4) junior current interest; (5) any residual to the junior capital account. An unpaid fee above the cap is not moved into senior interest. Unpaid senior interest carries forward without interest on interest."),
        ("records", "CASH CONTROL NOTES\nThe servicing team records collection dates and asset references before sending the cash file to the trustee. A buyer's promise to pay may be attached as a forecast, but must remain outside the distributable cash total. Reconciliation matches the bank statement to the file and explains outstanding items. Forecasts are useful for the next period's planning; they cannot fund the present distribution. Tax escrow belongs in its own ledger so an invoice paid from escrow does not appear again as an unrestricted cash expense."),
        ("page1", "\f"),
        ("reserve", "RESERVE TARGET\nThe target is 40 while the performance trigger is clear. It becomes 70 when the trigger is active. A refill uses the difference between the current reserve balance and the applicable target, with a floor of zero. A reserve already above target does not pay a negative refill; excess reserve is released only by a separately authorized release instruction."),
        ("trigger", "PERFORMANCE TRIGGER\nThe trigger becomes active when the three-month average delinquency ratio is strictly above 4.0%. A value exactly 4.0% does not activate it. While active, junior current interest and junior residual distributions are suspended; cash left after steps 1 through 3 remains in unrestricted cash. Junior unpaid current interest is recorded, but does not jump ahead of the reserve in the next period."),
        ("case", "DISTRIBUTION EXERCISE\nPeriod collections are 140, opening unrestricted cash is 10, and tax escrow is 20. A signed but unpaid sale is 30. The reserve balance is 15. The trustee requests 7 in fees, senior current interest is 50, senior interest arrears are 10, and junior current interest is 25. The three-month delinquency average is 4.2%. No reserve release instruction exists and no other deductions apply."),
        ("reports", "REPORTING REVIEW\nThe distribution notice should list cash available, each applied step, the ending reserve and retained unrestricted cash. Amounts withheld from junior distribution are not a payment to senior capital unless a separate capital repayment step is authorized. Staff should retain the unapproved draft and the signed final notice with different version labels. A reviewer may correct a transcription error before signing, but cannot move a restricted escrow balance into the waterfall to make a draft reconcile. The cap applies to the current trustee fee step; a requested fee above the cap is not permission to skip reserve replenishment."),
        ("page2", "\f"),
        ("cure", "CURE AND RELEASE\nAn active trigger clears only after the three-month average is at or below 3.0% on two consecutive monthly observation dates. One low month is insufficient. After cure, the ordinary target of 40 applies, but any release of reserve above 40 still needs the separate release instruction. Cure alone does not turn previously suspended junior interest into senior arrears."),
        ("exception", "RESERVE DRAW\nA liquidity draw may cover a shortfall in senior current interest only, after the trustee fee step. It cannot pay junior interest, senior interest arrears, or fees. The draw requires both trustee and oversight officer approval. A draw reduces the reserve balance used in the later refill step; it is not new period collections."),
        ("version", "VERSION REGISTER\nCE-8 released every residual to junior even when the trigger was active. CE-9 retains that residual in unrestricted cash. The new rule applies to distribution periods ending on or after 2026-09-01, including assets originated under CE-8. It does not reopen already completed earlier distributions. Reserve targets and the cure test are unchanged."),
        ("limits", "BOUNDARY\nThis memorandum contains no actual borrower identities, a tax withholding rate for investors, or a projected equipment sale price. The fictional amounts do not establish an investment yield, and a cash-flow calculation cannot supply missing tax terms."),
